                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Blink:Rogues, a fresh take on a thousand done before [/h1]\n\nBlink:Rogues is a relatively new top down shooter with a simple but unique twist, because the complexity of this game is rather simple this will be a short review but it will be a worthwhile one. \n\n[b] I know top down shooters! [/b]\n\nAlmost everyone knows what a top down shooter is like and hwo to play it, Blink isn’t any different than any other on that part, it features the same waves of enemies system where you have a base attack that always fires and some special attacks; this is a relatively common format in top down shooters. Luckily it’s not the same old stuff you’re used to: Blink is in fact always a split screen experience regardless if you play alone or with a friend, this is because of an important mechanic which is swapping your plane over to the other side of the screen to get extra points, health, ammo and dodge unbeatable waves of enemies. This is a fun concept as it makes the gameplay more dynamic and doesn’t have you falling asleep at your keyboard and it allows for pretty seamless dual player integration meaning that you can easily play it with a friend with the game barely changing. Is this a industry changer? No it’s not but it’s still a very fun mechanic to play around with. \n\n[b] Graphics and sounds [/b]\n\nDespite being a top down shooter Blink is actually rendered in Unreal Engine 4 which may seem a bit overkill at first but because it’s displayed at very small quantities should not only most pc’s cope with it but it also looks very pretty to look at it, at least for a top down shooter that is. Because everything is rendered in 3D and not as a 2D graphic it looks a lot more real as well and I enjoy that. \n\nWhen it comes to sounds it’s handled good but not exceptional, the constant firing mechanism doesn’t have an annoying noise and the soundtrack is all right for the subject but it’s not the best nor are the firing sounds the most entertaining and amazing to listen to for 20.000 times but they’re good enough for you to not want to cut off your ears\n\n[b] Conclusion [/b]\n\nBlink:Rogues is a fun little game with a proper storyline, although a bit cheesy, and nice animations and graphics to go with it. The gameplay doesn’t get too repetitive and it keeps being enjoyable for quite some time, offering seamless hotseat play as well makes it not just fun to play by yourself but fun to play with friends as well. For its measly 4 Euro price tag I would recommend it to play for most people if you’re into top down shooters with a pretty medium level of difficulty this is for you. \n",
